library "Patient Age Upper".

// UPPER-BOUND patient-age engine proof (#215). Two both-representation concepts (both
// comparators) + three decisions (incl. a negated one) let one $apply per (decision,case)
// prove each matrix cell. The engine-verified alternative to the INCORRECT `sem-not
// "Age 21 Or Older"` complement: under closed world an unknown age evaluates FALSE (deny).
//
// NOTE: the COMPUTE-ONLY lane (a `definition is` with no `code is`) is proven at the CQL
// emit level (crl unit tests, Todo 1) — a compute-only boolean returns a raw System.Boolean
// which the layered Interface's `.satisfied()` (defined over a truth-set) cannot wrap; that
// is a PRE-EXISTING, comparator-agnostic layered-emit limitation (the shipped `at least`
// compute-only guard hits it identically), orthogonal to #215. So the engine proof here is
// the BOTH-REP lane — which is exactly the KE's measured case.

// both-rep EXCLUSIVE under-21
concept "Under Twenty One":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `under-21`.
- source representation:
  - type is Patient.
  - value projection is age today under 21 years.

// both-rep INCLUSIVE at-most-21 (proves <= vs <: at age 21 this is TRUE, under-21 is FALSE)
concept "At Most Twenty One":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `at-most-21`.
- source representation:
  - type is Patient.
  - value projection is age today at most 21 years.

decision "Pediatric Eligibility Determination":
first:
- when "Under Twenty One" then recommend activity "certify.Approve".
- otherwise then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".

decision "Inclusive Boundary Determination":
first:
- when "At Most Twenty One" then recommend activity "certify.Approve".
- otherwise then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".

// NEGATED both-rep: for UNKNOWN age the truth-set is empty -> FALSE -> `not FALSE` = TRUE,
// so a decision-layer `when not <under-21>` FIRES for unknown age (treats unknown as
// not-under-21). This is the AUTHORED decision-layer negation, distinct from the inference
// -layer `sem-not` that produced the #215 bug (which emit refuses over a definition-is).
decision "Negated Both Rep Determination":
first:
- when not "Under Twenty One" then recommend activity "certify.Approve".
- otherwise then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".

activity "certify.Approve":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Eligibility: APPROVE.`.
activity "not-certify.Deny":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Eligibility: DENY.`.
